                        "review": "[i]playthrough in progress[/i]\nThe writing is nice - consistent, competent, with distinct manner of speech for different characters, and leaning onto humour and sexual innuendo, but without explicit erotic content. The controls are rebindable, the saving is adequate (multiple save slots + auto-saving). The art and design are fantastic - expressive and easy to read. There are content warnings for some of the routes and the ability to skip them. Unfortunately, no ability to skip the routes where all options show the avatar's lack of digital literacy. The sound design is done well, including the full VA and it is one of the rare cases where it is a good fit. \n\nThere is an overarching plot, but the idea of finding 100 NPC and completing their quests in a relatively small house is appealing as is. The topics of job insecurity and the lack of unionisation, going throughout the story, are not exclusive to the US, but more prevalent there. \n\nI had some issue with the camera shaking, but it seems to have passed after a few minutes and switching the mouse to the lowest sensitivity.",
